    {
      "id": "a1_u04_l02",
      "level": "A1",
      "unit": 4,
      "title": "Il et elle",
      "description": "Talk about other people with il and elle, and describe what they are like.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 13,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "He and she",
              "body": "\"Il\" means \"he\" and \"elle\" means \"she\". With them, être becomes \"est\" and avoir becomes \"a\": \"Il est grand\" (He is tall), \"Elle a dix ans\" (She is ten). This is how you talk about your family members.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Il est grand.", "english": "He is tall." },
                { "french": "Elle est gentille.", "english": "She is kind." },
                { "french": "Mon frère a huit ans.", "english": "My brother is eight years old." },
                { "french": "Elle s'appelle Emma.", "english": "Her name is Emma." },
                { "french": "Il est beau.", "english": "He is handsome." },
                { "french": "Elle est sympa.", "english": "She is nice." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "heading": "Describing people",
              "body": "Three useful adjectives: grand (tall/big), petit (short/small), gentil (kind/nice). When describing a woman or girl, add an -e: grande, petite — and gentil doubles its l: gentille.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Mon père est grand.", "english": "My father is tall." },
                { "french": "Ma sœur est petite.", "english": "My sister is short." },
                { "french": "Ma mère est très gentille.", "english": "My mother is very kind." },
                { "french": "Mon grand-père est vieux.", "english": "My grandfather is old." },
                { "french": "Elle a les yeux bleus.", "english": "She has blue eyes." }
              ],
              "tip": "The final consonant often becomes audible in the feminine: grand = \"grahn\" but grande = \"grahnd\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "vocabulary",
          "title": "Vocabulary",
          "items": [
