      "title": "Chez nous",
      "description": "Talk about life at home with your family — and your pets.",
      "estimatedMinutes": 12,
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "title": "Learn",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "heading": "At our place",
              "body": "\"Chez\" means \"at the home of\": chez moi (at my place), chez nous (at our place), chez mes parents (at my parents' place). It's one of the most useful little words in French.",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Chez nous, nous sommes cinq.", "english": "At our place, there are five of us." },
                { "french": "J'habite chez mes parents.", "english": "I live at my parents' place." },
                { "french": "Viens chez moi !", "english": "Come to my place!" },
                { "french": "Chez moi, c'est petit.", "english": "My place is small." },
                { "french": "Nous habitons dans un appartement.", "english": "We live in an apartment." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "heading": "Pets",
              "body": "Many French families have pets: un chien (a dog) or un chat (a cat). To say you love them, use \"aimer\" (to like/love) or the stronger \"adorer\": \"J'adore mon chat !\"",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Nous avons un chien.", "english": "We have a dog." },
                { "french": "J'ai un chat. Il s'appelle Minou.", "english": "I have a cat. His name is Minou." },
                { "french": "J'adore les animaux !", "english": "I love animals!" },
                { "french": "Le lapin mange une carotte.", "english": "The rabbit eats a carrot." },
                { "french": "L'oiseau chante dans le jardin.", "english": "The bird sings in the garden." }
              ],
              "tip": "The plural of \"animal\" is irregular: un animal, des animaux."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
