            {
              "heading": "Nous sommes, nous avons",
              "body": "To speak for the whole family, use \"nous\" (we): nous sommes (we are) and nous avons (we have). \"Nous sommes quatre\" is the natural way to say \"there are four of us\".",
              "examples": [
                { "french": "Nous sommes quatre.", "english": "There are four of us." },
                { "french": "Nous avons deux chats.", "english": "We have two cats." },
                { "french": "Nous habitons à Marseille.", "english": "We live in Marseille." },
                { "french": "Nous sommes ensemble.", "english": "We are together." },
                { "french": "Nous avons un oiseau et deux poissons.", "english": "We have a bird and two fish." }
              ],
              "tip": "Link \"nous avons\": the s sounds like z — noo-zah-VOHN."
            }
          ]
